	Developing Classical UI Features into an Authority Legend for American Social and Cultural Capital (Precursors to an American Social Credit System)
                     
Likes - For some hegemonies that post media in digital spaces, 'likes' can be an indicator of affiliation or endorsement, especially if the hegemonies represented in those digital spaces are consistently portrayed with high social and cultural capital in fictional as opposed to non-fictional media.
If moral entrepreneurship remains active within any digital infrastructure, future progeny may begin to use likes as a gateway to study the users that gave likes as oppose to measuring how many like the media received.

Comments - Comments may be used to evaluate the communicative competence of those that comment on a piece of media as a means to evaluate the communicative competence of the user that posted the media.
If moral entrepreneurship remains active within any digital infrastructure, comments can serve as a means to audit engagement and to form their own methods of rhetorical analysis, which can incorporate the creation of protologisms and neologisms for specific circles.

Tagged - Organized collectives or even individuals that face risks and liabilities with engaging in indiscriminate affiliation may view tagged images as a formal connection to an organized collective or personal life.
If moral entrepreneurs successfully maintain a moral panic within any digital infrastructure, future progeny may begin to congregate and vote on who's tagged and not tagged in certain infrastructures.

Followers - Some hegemonies may audit followers as a means to identify intersecting or contrasting dogma of a user and their followers. As well as to spot parallels or even contrasts in a user and their follower's pedagogy.
Future progeny may use followers as a means to seamlessly adapt the "Six Degrees of Separation" concept into an automated tool that can identify local grapevines as they're digitally documented through shared followers.

Following - Some hegemonies may see profiles or pages that a user is following as a direct indicator of a pursued interest, personal projection, or an interpretation of a user's real-life behavior, attitude, orientation, and political alignment.
Future progeny may use followers as a means to associate themselves with specific brands, influencers, content creators, political figures, and corporate entities as a means to publicly display alignment with their local hegemonies.